      "side": 1,
      "message": "Heads up: the badfish backend set_bios_attribute (tools/external/badfish.py:373-374) does a patch_bios then calls reboot_server() internally. So when the bootmode actually differs, this line sets the BIOS attribute and reboots the host, and then reboot_for_rebuild calls reboot_server(graceful\u003dFalse) again a few lines later. That\u0027s a double reboot on every rebuild where bootmode is mismatched. The mock tests won\u0027t catch it since they assert set_bios_attribute was awaited but not that it reboots. Consider either not calling reboot_server() again after a successful bootmode set, or calling a setter that doesn\u0027t reboot (e.g. patch_bios only), so the existing reboot at the end of reboot_for_rebuild stays the single one.",
